                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>4 - Gap to Market</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>: The report allows to assess and simulate the average comp ratio based on base salary, LTIP and total compensation for each department</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>5 - Gap to Market by Level</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>: The report allows to assess and simulate the average comp ratio based on base salary, LTIP and total compensation for each job level</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>6 - Pay Mix</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>: The report allows to assess and simulate the average pay mix for each job level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='14'>Objectives</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>This dashboard answers the following questions:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>1. What would be the average comp ratio if we increase the midpoint of salary bands?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>2. What would be the average comp ratio if we increase salaries in Tech?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>3. What would be the pay bill if we increase salaries in Tech?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>4. What would be the pay bill if we force all salaries to be at least 90% of the midpoint?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>5. What would be the average LTIP comp ratio if we increase the LTIP target?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>6. What would be the average LTIP comp ratio if we increase the LTIP granted amount?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>7. What would be the average LTIP comp ratio if we bring all employees to their LTIP target?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>8. What would be the average LTIP comp ratio if we modify the targets?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>9. What is the current comp ratio distribution based on total compensation?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>10. How would it change based on changes on base salaries and LTIP?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>11. What is the gap to market in each department?</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Open Sans' fontsize='11'>12. What is the gap to market for each job level?</run>
